# {{.Name}}

A Millstream action written against the action protocol directly, without an SDK. `main.py` implements it with the
Python 3 standard library only; any language that reads and writes lines of JSON works the same way. A POSIX shell
implementation is not offered: parsing JSON robustly in `sh` is not realistic.

The full contract is the [action protocol](https://github.com/monolithiclab/millstream/blob/main/docs/protocol.md).
In short:

## Framing

- The engine writes to the action's stdin and reads its stdout: one JSON object per line, UTF-8, ending in `\n`, at
  most 8 MiB per line. Nothing else may be written to stdout.
- Every object has a `type`; keys are lowerCamelCase. Ignore the keys you do not know.
- stderr is free-form logging; never write payload values there.
- `MILLSTREAM_WORKDIR` names a directory for the process: input artifacts are placed in it, output artifacts are
  written to it.

## Messages

Engine to action:

```json
{"type":"hello","protocol":1,"action":"{{.Name}}","version":"0.1.0","config":{"greeting":"Hello"},"vars":{}}
{"type":"item","delivery":"dl_1","id":"it_1","key":"","payload":{"name":"Ada"},"artifacts":[],"run":{"id":"run_1","trigger":"adhoc","startedAt":"2026-10-14T06:00:00Z","revision":"5c1d"},"attempt":1,"idempotencyKey":"7e2b"}
{"type":"shutdown"}
```

Action to engine:

```json
{"type":"ready"}
{"type":"emit","delivery":"dl_1","payload":{"greeting":"Hello, Ada!"}}
{"type":"metric","delivery":"dl_1","name":"names_greeted","value":1}
{"type":"done","delivery":"dl_1"}
{"type":"error","delivery":"dl_1","message":"the item has no name","retryable":false}
```

1. Answer `hello` with `ready`, within 10 seconds.
2. Answer each `item` with any number of `emit` and `metric` messages for its delivery, then exactly one `done` or
   `error`. Outputs are published on `done` only. Several outputs must each carry a distinct `key`.
3. Write nothing between deliveries. Exit with status 0 on `shutdown` or at the end of stdin.

An `error` with `retryable: true` is retried with backoff; `false` dead-letters the item at once. A malformed line, an
unknown `type` or a message for another delivery is a protocol violation: the engine kills the process and retries.

## Checking it

```sh
millstream test action .                  # the fixtures under tests/
millstream test action . --conformance    # the protocol conformance suite
```
